{{ImageSplit|image=Thunderwing_Titan_artwork.jpg|alt=Thunderwing Titan|text=The '''Thunderwing Titan''' is a colossal winged boss that rules the flying islands of '''Reedwind'''. It is one of the seven Major [[World Bosses]], and unlike most of them it has no fixed spawn time. Players summon it themselves.

{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=Level|type=info|tag=Required|You need to be level 50 to take part.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Duration|type=info|tag=2 hours|Thunderwing Titan stays for 2 hours after it is called.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Cooldown|type=control|tag=48 hours|Summoning the boss has a cooldown of 48 hours.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Where|type=info|tag=Reedwind|Reedwind. Interact with the built faction tower to get the {{BuffLink|20883}} buff, which lets you fight.}}
}}}}

== Preparation ==
To fight Thunderwing Titan you need to prepare some special items first.
{{InfoGrid|{{InfoCard|title=Required|type=danger|tag=Wings|wide=yes|Bring {{Item|ItemID=15621|amount=10}} to get the Wings needed to take part in the fight.}}}}
{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=Optional|type=reward|tag=Health Potion|{{RecipeBox|9469}}}}
{{InfoCard|title=Optional|type=reward|tag=Mana Potion|{{RecipeBox|9470}}}}}}

== Summoning ==
Thunderwing Titan is called from a floating island in Reedwind.

{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=1. Build the tower|type=info|tag=Faction|Players use {{Item|ItemID=42590|amount=5}} at a time to build their faction's tower in the zone. A fully built tower requires {{Item|ItemID=42590|amount=5000}}.}}
{{InfoCard|title=2. Take the portal|type=control|tag=Level 50|Interact with the built tower to get the {{BuffLink|20883}} buff.}}
{{InfoCard|title=3. Summon|type=reward|tag=Cost|Summoning consumes {{Item|ItemID=41561|amount=1}} and {{Item|ItemID=26880|amount=10}}.}}
}}

{{CallOut|title=Patch 1.2.8|type=info|text=Patch 1.2.8 (May 2024) made Thunderwing Titan easier to attempt and to defeat.}}

== The fight ==
The fight takes place in the air. Everyone fights on '''Titan's Wings''' that are handed out for the fight, and each fighter needs {{Item|ItemID=15621|amount=10}} to get a pair. The wings have their own skills and potions, so your normal skill bar does not matter much here.

{{InfoGrid|
{{InfoCard|title=Wings|type=info|tag=Pick one|{{Item|ItemID=41542}} are for melee and ranged fighters and {{Item|ItemID=42566}} are for healers and mages.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Orbs|type=danger|tag=Dodge|Blue and red orbs fly out in flurries. Dodge them, because they hit very hard.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Adds|type=danger|tag=Kill fast|The boss summons small monsters. If they are left alive they turn into healing orbs for Thunderwing Titan, so kill them quickly.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Wing attack|type=danger|tag=Stay clear|Getting too close to the wings pushes you away and deals damage.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Pull|type=control|tag=Crowd control|The boss can drag everyone in a large radius towards itself.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Healing shield|type=heal|tag=Keep up damage|Thunderwing Titan curls into a shielded orb that can't be interrupted and heals itself. Keep your damage high enough between heals so you do not lose ground.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Slow and damage over time|type=debuff|tag=Bring potions|Gliders near Thunderwing Titan are slowed and take damage over time, so bring healing potions.}}
{{InfoCard|title=Feather orbs|type=reward|tag=Pick up|Feather orbs drop during the fight, and picking one up gives you a special skill.}}
}}

{{CallOut|title=Tips|
* Bring as many people as you can on the first attempts, because the fight takes some learning.
* Kill the adds fast and stay clear of the orbs.
* Carry enough {{Item|ItemID=42634}}, since glider healing can't keep up with the damage over time.
* Mages can bring a Greatclub as a swap to make their healing skill more potent when needed.
}}

